## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | BLOCKING | lib/src/cloud/drive_sync_engine.dart | 🚨 blocking remote tombstone for a locally missing file crashes drivesyncengine pull and permanently stalls drive sync pullremotedelete drive sync engine dart 299 calls env remove path absolute without force true — per the executionenv remove contract a missing path is an error without force — and pull runs pullremoteitem in an unguarded loop before the cas save so one tombstone aborts the entire pull and nothing including the cursor is persisted reproduced against the real engine memorydrivesyncstore memoryexecutionenv provider feed containing deleted true for drive notes never here txt pull threw fileerror notfound drive notes never here txt no such file or directory real world trigger another device creates and deletes a file between this device s pulls or a first pull whose delta feed contains historical tombstones every subsequent pull replays the same tombstone fails at the same point and never advances state — drive sync is stuck for that mount until manual intervention fix env remove path absolute force true here and consider the same at line 111 in enqueuedelete for the double delete case plus a regression test that pulls a tombstone for a path never materialized locally |
| F2 | open | BLOCKING | lib/src/product/fa_product_config.dart | 🚨 blocking themepack string values bypass the markup filter and land as live script markup in the branded product config js the themepack validation fa product config dart 193 checks only shapes and keys name version are string colors is a map no wallpaper code script … keys — the values are never passed through the text filter that correctly rejects for displayname description publicprofile then embeds the raw themepack via jsonencode into product config js which index html loads as a classic script src — and dart s jsonencode does not escape so any script inside a value terminates the script element early and the rest executes as markup this contradicts the invariant this pr itself documents at docs product cloud md 70 no profile becomes executable trusted markup reproduced through the real code path faproductconfig fromjson → stagebrandedshell profile accepted emitted file js window faproductprofile productid host product themepack name x version 1 0 0 colors dark accent script script alert document cookie script the same hole exists via themepack name its slug must merely equal themepackid which any slug shaped id satisfies text fields are already protected so this is an inconsistent boundary in exactly the validator the p0 milestone advertises profiles are programmatically generated for hosts so a benign template value tom jerry default breaks the shell silently and a hostile profile gets script execution in the branded app origin fix either or both validate every themepack string value with the same text rules as displayname or escape the script context on emission jsonencode replaceall for product config js add a rejection test mirroring the existing valid displayname script … case |
| F3 | open | IMPORTANT | lib/src/cloud/cloud_session_synchronizer.dart | ⚠️ important the cloud session sync cursor is dead state — never consulted and never advanced two compounding defects make the persisted cursor field non functional 1 line 198 starts listing from the local null never from the persisted snapshot cursor — compare the sibling drivesyncengine pull which passes cursor snapshot cursor 2 the final save line 231 passes the loop exit cursor which is always null the do while only exits when cursor null and cloudsessionsnapshot copywith uses semantics so copywith cursor null keeps the old value the stored cursor is therefore never written with a real value either consequence every pull re lists the entire remote session set all pages and relies on alreadymaterialized to skip downloads — correctness holds but the delta pagination contract of remotesessionprovider list scope cursor is never used and the cost grows with the remote session count there is no test asserting cursor persistence the only cursor mention in cloud session sync test dart is a fake provider parameter fix seed the listing from snapshot cursor advance it per page persisting nextcursor even when a later page fails if partial progress should survive restarts and give copywith a way to store an explicit null sentinel or a setcursor parameter add a test pull page 1 of 2 → snapshot cursor page 1 cursor second pull resumes instead of full scanning |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

